{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779637677,"nonce":"fZOGa5ELLpqtPVGZSlGN8/eCbHw=","title":"Project meta coordination: cross-project / workflow concerns","message":"Coordination surface for cross-project / workflow concerns surfaced during Feedbax work. This body is intentionally minimal: comments index cross-cutting concerns; the actual fixes live in the destination repos.\n\n## What goes here\n\nWhen working on Feedbax or Feedbax Studio, you may surface concerns affecting:\n- Mandible auth flow, issue tracking, hooks, coordination scaffolding, or dashboard behavior\n- RLRMP or other downstream research projects consuming Feedbax contracts\n- Dotfiles/global agent workflow\n- General workflow/tooling patterns that are not Feedbax-internal bugs\n\nFile the actual issue in the destination repo when the fix belongs elsewhere. Then comment here with: destination repo + issue ID, one-line rationale, and optional link back to the Feedbax work that surfaced it.\n\n## What does not go here\n\nFeedbax-internal architecture/design concerns should go to the relevant Feedbax design or umbrella issue. Bugs/features entirely within Feedbax should use normal issues.\n\n## Related Feedbax coordination surfaces\n\n- `93f79f2` — Feedbax Studio design coordination.\n- `8d94424` — Feedbax design coordination.\n- `a3e46d5` — active Studio product-depth / Feedbax contract sequencing umbrella.\n\nLabel: `coordination`. Do not reference this issue in commit `Bug:` trailers; it is an index for cross-project context, not an implementation closure target.","files":null}]}